I was in MENSA for two years (1982-4), met a few interesting people (in
person and postally), and suffered severe blows to my elitist views, which
I have incorporated into my theories as a conclusion that taking the top
2% in intelligence tests is not as efficient a filter against stupidity as
I would have hoped.  The stated purpose of getting really smart people
together seems to be served better by indirect approaches (like
science-fiction fandom and this group) than by the direct approach of Mensa.

